            <ArticleTitle>Cutaneous Chromomycosis with Pulmonary Geotrichosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>331-333</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An 80 year old farmer had cutaneous chromomycosis on the lateral aspect of right foot. He had associated pulmonary pathology caused by another fungus Geotrichum candidum simulating miliary tuberculosis. Complete regression of the pulmonary lesions and partial regression of the cutaneous lesions was observed with iodide therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
